ha-wattpilot — Home Assistant integration for Fronius Wattpilot

This project interoperates with a reverse-engineered WebSocket API.
Protocol knowledge and property semantics build on prior work:

- joscha82/wattpilot (MIT) — original protocol reverse engineering
- mk-maddin — original Home Assistant Wattpilot integration concept (Apache-2.0)
- ruaan-deysel/wattpilot-api (MIT) — the async client library. Version
  1.4.0 was adopted into this project under custom_components/wattpilot/api/,
  which carries its MIT licence text, and is maintained here since. Only the
  modules this integration uses came along (client, auth, definition, models,
  exceptions, utils and the API definition resource); mqtt, shell and
  discovery did not. Changes against 1.4.0 are marked in the source with a
  `wattpilot:` comment.
- ruaan-deysel/ha-wattpilot (Apache-2.0) — the integration this project
  replaces. No source code was copied from the Apache-2.0 project; only
  interoperability facts (property keys, enum values, unique-id suffixes)
  are reused for drop-in compatibility.

